<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kang Tai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kang Tai was an envoy of Eastern Wu who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhu-ying">Zhu Ying</a>, was sent by the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a> to Funan in mainland South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> in the mid-3rd century. His account of the journey, known through quotations in later works, is one of the earliest descriptions of Funan, recording its founding legend and its trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
